      "summaries": {
        "en": "Unciv is an open-source remake of Civilization V for Android and desktop, built with Kotlin and LibGDX. It faithfully recreates the classic 4X strategy experience—explore, expand, exploit, and exterminate—with a clean, pixel-art interface. Technically, it demonstrates how to port a complex turn-based game to mobile using cross-platform frameworks. You can play it on Android or desktop, fork the code to study game AI or mod the rules, or contribute to its active community. Perfect for learning game development or enjoying Civ on the go.",
        "zh": "Unciv 是一款基于 Kotlin 和 LibGDX 框架的开源《文明 V》复刻版，支持 Android 和桌面平台。它完整还原了经典的 4X 策略玩法——探索、扩张、开发、征服——并以简洁的像素风格呈现。技术亮点在于展示了如何利用跨平台框架将复杂的回合制策略游戏移植到移动端，同时保持流畅体验。你可以直接安装游玩，或 fork 代码研究游戏 AI 逻辑、修改规则模组，甚至参与社区贡献。对于想学习游戏开发或随时来一局文明的玩家，Unciv 是绝佳的开源参考。",
        "es": "Unciv is an open-source remake of Civilization V for Android and desktop, built with Kotlin and LibGDX. It faithfully recreates the classic 4X strategy experience—explore, expand, exploit, and exterminate—with a clean, pixel-art interface. Technically, it demonstrates how to port a complex turn-based game to mobile using cross-platform frameworks. You can play it on Android or desktop, fork the code to study game AI or mod the rules, or contribute to its active community. Perfect for learning game development or enjoying Civ on the go.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "Unciv stands out for 4x, 4x-strategy-game, and android in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Unciv is an open-source remake of Civilization V for Android and desktop, built with Kotlin and LibGDX. It faithfully recreates the classic 4X strategy experience—explore, expand, exploit, and exterminate—with a clean, pixel-art interface. Technically, it demonstrates how to port a complex turn-based game to mobile using cross-platform frameworks. You can play it on Android or desktop, fork the code to study game AI or mod the rules, or contribute to its active community. Perfect for learning game development or enjoying Civ on the go.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/yairm210/Unciv for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
