      "summaries": {
        "en": "rlm is a general plug-and-play inference library for Recursive Language Models (RLMs), simplifying the deployment of models that iterate over their own outputs for enhanced reasoning. Its key technical insight is supporting multiple sandbox environments, allowing safe and flexible execution of recursive inference loops. Practically, you can use rlm to experiment with RLMs for tasks like multi-step reasoning or self-correction, integrating it into existing Python projects with minimal setup.",
        "zh": "rlm是一个通用的即插即用推理库，专为递归语言模型（RLM）设计，解决了递归模型部署复杂的问题。其核心技术亮点是支持多种沙箱环境，使得模型在递归推理循环中能够安全、灵活地执行。通过rlm，开发者可以轻松实验RLM的多步推理和自我修正能力，只需简单集成到现有Python项目中即可。无论是研究递归模型的推理机制，还是构建需要迭代思考的应用，rlm都提供了高效的工具。",
        "es": "rlm is a general plug-and-play inference library for Recursive Language Models (RLMs), simplifying the deployment of models that iterate over their own outputs for enhanced reasoning. Its key technical insight is supporting multiple sandbox environments, allowing safe and flexible execution of recursive inference loops. Practically, you can use rlm to experiment with RLMs for tasks like multi-step reasoning or self-correction, integrating it into existing Python projects with minimal setup.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "rlm gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "rlm is a general plug-and-play inference library for Recursive Language Models (RLMs), simplifying the deployment of models that iterate over their own outputs for enhanced reasoning. Its key technical insight is supporting multiple sandbox environments, allowing safe and flexible execution of recursive inference loops. Practically, you can use rlm to experiment with RLMs for tasks like multi-step reasoning or self-correction, integrating it into existing Python projects with minimal setup.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/alexzhang13/rlm for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
